# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# The F4 stops talking (LV side lost: hv0.sim_f4_dead): the HV side runs
# from the DC bus, so the F3 brakes on its own (hv0.brake_on_loss, pmsm
# template): the virtual resistor of shared/vbrake.h in its own frame, as
# stm32f303/src/comps/ls.c does, until the current has died down (~3.8
# rad, 6 mm). The current stays under 0.9 * max_ac_cur.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
hv0.sim_f4_dead = 1
@sample hv0.abs_cur 0.001 0.05
hv0.sim_f3_brake
run 0.25
hv0.sim_dist
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_f3_brake
@expect hv0.sim_f3_brake[1] == 1
@expect max|hv0.abs_cur| < 9
@expect hv0.sim_dist ~ 3.8 0.6
@expect hv0.sim_vel[2] ~ 0 0.5
@expect hv0.sim_f3_brake[2] == 0
